      "text": "The Catatumbo Delta is located southwest of Lake Maracaibo (13,280 km²). The delta covers 226,330 hectares and was declared the Ciénagas de Juan Manuel National Park (Ciénagas del Catatumbo) in 1991.\n\nEarly transfer to the airport. Flight and meeting with our best local guide.\n\nDeparture by 4x4 vehicles towards the city of Santa Bárbara, Zulia State. Stop for lunch.\n\nArrival at the pier and boat trip by motor canoe along the Concha River. Along the way, you may see Tonino dolphins, howler monkeys (araguatos), various birds, iguanas, and local crocodiles known as babas. You’ll also experience the traditional “tricky” fishing for blue crabs on Lake Maracaibo.\n\nArrival at the stilt hotel (palafito lodge). Traditional dinner featuring grilled blue crabs.\n\nAt night, you’ll observe the unique Catatumbo Lightning phenomenon — a spectacular natural display of continuous lightning over the delta.\n\nOvernight in hammocks (the lodge provides showers and all basic amenities).\n\nMeals: light breakfast, lunch, dinner"
    },
